course: everyday
lesson: 63
title: Guinea pigs, hamsters and fish
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Small pets have very different needs, so before you look after one you learn what its own kind needs, not what a person or another animal needs.
explain: Guinea pigs are herd animals that need a friend and fresh vegetables every day for vitamin C; adult Syrian hamsters are the opposite and must live alone, because they fight.
explain: Small animals are fragile: a hamster can be killed by a fall from a short height, so you hold it in two cupped hands sitting close to the floor.
explain: Fish live in their water, so whatever goes in it stays there: uneaten food rots and poisons the water, and that is why you feed only what they eat in a couple of minutes.
explain: A girl in Michigan wins a goldfish at a fair. She does not tip it into a bowl or the pond; her family brings it home only because they already have a proper tank ready.
explain: A boy in Texas woke his hamster in the daytime by poking it; the startled hamster bit his finger hard.
explain: A girl in Scotland overfed her goldfish and never cleaned the tank; the water went cloudy and smelly and the fish became ill and died.
fact: Guinea pigs cannot make their own vitamin C, so they need fresh vegetables such as pepper or leafy greens every day.
fact: Guinea pigs are herd animals, so at least two should live together.
fact: Adult Syrian hamsters fight, sometimes badly, so each one lives alone.
fact: A hamster wheel must be big enough for its back to stay straight, or it can hurt its spine.
fact: You hold a hamster in two cupped hands and sit close to the floor, because a short fall can kill it.
fact: In a hamster ball a hamster cannot escape, can get too hot and may crash into things, so it is used only briefly with an adult, never near stairs, or not at all.
fact: Hamsters carry food in their cheek pouches to store it in their nest.
fact: When cleaning a hamster cage you spot clean often (clear out just the dirty bits) and leave some old bedding so it still smells like home.
fact: Fish should get only as much food as they eat in a couple of minutes, because leftovers rot and poison the water.
fact: Tapping on aquarium glass makes a loud, frightening noise for fish.
fact: A fish floating at the top or gasping may be ill or in dirty water short of oxygen.
fact: Pet fish must never be released into ponds or rivers, because they can spread disease and harm native wildlife (the wild animals that belong there).
fact: Goldfish can remember things for months and learn feeding times; the three-second memory is a myth.
fact: Hamsters sleep in the day, wake up in the evening, and often bite if they are woken suddenly.
fact: Too much fish food makes the water dirty, and dirty water can kill fish.
exercise: Your guinea pigs squeak loudly whenever you open the fridge. What is a good thing to give them? | A little fresh pepper or leafy greens | A slice of cheese | A spoonful of yoghurt | Some crisps
exercise: Why do guinea pigs need fresh vegetables every day? | Their bodies cannot make vitamin C | Vegetables keep their fur from falling out | They cannot drink water | Vegetables keep them awake at night
exercise: How many guinea pigs should live together? | At least two | Only one on its own | Exactly one with a hamster | As many as fit in a small box
exercise: Your friend wants to put her two adult Syrian hamsters in one cage so they are not lonely. What is right? | Keep Syrian hamsters alone, because adults fight | Put them together, hamsters love company and get lonely on their own | Put them together but only at night | Put them together with a guinea pig
exercise: A hamster runs in its wheel with its back bent like a banana. What should change? | Use a bigger wheel so its back stays straight | Take away the wheel forever | Make the wheel spin faster so its back stretches out | Put the wheel in the sun
exercise: How should you hold a hamster? | In two cupped hands, sitting close to the floor | By the scruff of its neck, standing up tall so it feels safe | By its tail, so it cannot run off | Pinched between two fingers
exercise: What is the safest choice about a hamster ball? | Use it only briefly with an adult, away from stairs, or skip it | Leave the hamster in it all afternoon, so it gets lots of exercise and fresh air | Roll it down the stairs for fun | Put it outside in the sun
exercise: Your hamster's cheeks are puffed up and full. What is it doing? | Carrying food to store in its nest | Getting ready to bite your finger hard | Showing that it is very ill and needs a vet | Holding its breath so it can go swimming
exercise: How should you clean a hamster cage? | Spot clean often and leave some old bedding so it smells like home | Throw away all the bedding every day and scrub everything with perfume and soap | Never clean it at all | Clean it once a year only
exercise: Your fish rush to the top and look hungry. How much should you feed them? | Only what they eat in a couple of minutes | As much as they will eat all day | A full spoon every hour | Enough to cover the bottom of the tank
exercise: Why should you not tap on the aquarium glass? | The noise is loud and frightening for fish | It makes the glass dirty | The fish might jump out | It makes the water in the tank much too cold for them
exercise: Your fish is floating at the top and gasping. What should you do? | Tell an adult and check the water | Tap the glass to wake it | Add lots more food | Leave it, fish often do this when they are sleepy
exercise: Your family is moving and cannot take the pet fish. Should you let them go in a river? | No, they can spread disease and harm native wildlife | Yes, fish are always happier in rivers than in tanks at home | Yes, but only goldfish | Yes, if the river is warm
exercise: Is it true that a goldfish has only a three-second memory? | No, goldfish can remember things for months | Yes, so it forgets you at once | Yes, but only when it is asleep | No, goldfish remember nothing at all, not even for a second
exercise: You win a goldfish at a fair. When should you take it home? | Only if you are ready with a proper tank | Always, in a small bowl on the windowsill | Always, and then tip it into the garden pond | Only if it fits in a small drinking glass
test: A boy in Manchester buys two guinea pigs but feeds them only dry pellets and water. What is missing? | Fresh vegetables for vitamin C every day | Meat for protein | Milk for strong bones | Nothing, pellets and water are all that guinea pigs need
test: A girl in Perth wants to hold her hamster while standing on a chair. Why is this a bad idea? | A fall even from a short height can kill a hamster | Hamsters get dizzy when held up high | The hamster will want to climb the chair legs and run off | Standing makes the hamster sleepy
test: A family in Ontario cleans the hamster cage, throws away every bit of bedding and adds new scented bedding. Why might the hamster be stressed? | Its home no longer smells familiar | The cage is now too clean to sleep in | Hamsters only like dirty, smelly cages | Scented bedding makes hamsters hungry
test: Which pair of pets should NOT share one cage? | Two adult Syrian hamsters | Two guinea pigs | Two rabbits | Two budgies
test: A boy feeds his fish four times as much as they can eat. After a few days the water is cloudy and the fish are sick. Why? | The uneaten food rotted and poisoned the water | Fish get sick from being too full | The fish got fat and could not swim | The bright light shining on the leftover food turned it cloudy
test: Why is releasing a pet goldfish into a lake bad for nature? | It can spread disease and harm the wild animals living there | The goldfish will be lonely | The lake water is far too clean and cold for goldfish to live in | Goldfish cannot swim in big water
test: Fish in a school aquarium gather at the front every morning before the teacher feeds them. What does this show? | Fish can learn and remember feeding times | Fish get scared of children | Fish always swim to the front | Fish forget everything in a few seconds, so it is just chance
test: A hamster has been rolling around in a hamster ball for an hour on a hot day. What could happen? | It could get too hot because it cannot escape | It will learn to steer the ball | It will get fitter and happier with every lap | Nothing, the ball keeps it cool
test: Why does a hamster need a wheel that is large? | A small wheel bends its back and can hurt its spine | Large wheels are quieter at night | Hamsters like to sleep in their wheels | Small wheels make hamsters run too fast and get very dizzy
test: gonna get 1 guinea pig, just the one, cheaper innit | Get at least two, they are herd animals | One is best, so that it bonds only with you | One is fine if you play with it every day | Get one now and another one in a few years when it's older
test: my mate reckons goldfish forget everything after 3 secs. true? | No, goldfish can remember things for months | Yes, three seconds is all they remember | Yes, that is why they swim in circles | No, they remember for about ten seconds
test: put loads of food in the tank so he dont go hungry over the weekend | No, give only what he eats in a couple of minutes | Yes, extra food keeps the water fresh | Yes, fish stop eating when they are full, so it'll last | Yes, leftovers sink and do no harm
test: don't want the fish anymore, can we tip him in the pond at the park | No, pet fish can spread disease to wild animals | Yes, he will be much happier in the pond with the ducks | Yes, if the pond is big enough | Yes, but only in the summer
test: hamster's asleep but i wanna play now | Let it sleep and play in the evening | Poke it gently until it wakes up and plays | Shake the cage a little so it wakes up | Pick it up gently while it sleeps, it won't even notice
test: fish look hungry so i put loads of food in | Give only a little, too much makes the water dirty | More food makes them grow | Fish stop eating when full | Put in food every hour so they never ever get hungry
test: Noah says guinea pigs are fine living alone forever. true? | No, guinea pigs need company of their own kind | Yes, they hate other guinea pigs | Yes, if they have a toy | Yes, unless they squeak at night, that means they're lonely
test: heard Josh's two hamsters had a massive fight and one died, his mum said they were brothers | Real lesson: adult Syrian hamsters fight, so each lives alone | Real lesson: hamster brothers always get along | It proves hamsters are dangerous to people | It is gossip, so two hamsters can share a cage
test: my mate says fish should get loads of food so they never get hungry | Wrong; give only what they eat in a couple of minutes, as leftovers rot | He is right, more food is always better | He is right, fish are always hungry | He is right, if you clean the tank daily
test: Mia's guinea pig died and someone said she killed it by not feeding it, should i tell people | No; it is unkind, likely untrue, and she is probably sad | Yes, because pets die from hunger | Yes, so she never gets another pet | Yes, and add that she did not care and forgot about it for weeks
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the dietary requirement of guinea pigs? | They cannot produce vitamin C and require fresh vegetables daily | They require only dry pellets and water | They produce vitamin C abundantly | They must be fed meat once a week
exam: Identify the reason for which guinea pigs ought to be kept at least in pairs. | They are herd animals | They fight when kept alone | They require each other for warmth only | Single guinea pigs cannot eat
exam: It being given that a hamster cage is cleaned, select the practice consistent with established guidance. | Some old bedding should be retained so that the cage still smells of home | All bedding should be replaced with scented material | The cage should be washed with strong bleach, scrubbed thoroughly and dried in the sun | The hamster should be moved permanently
exam: Select the response that is consistent with established guidance concerning the holding of a hamster. | In two cupped hands whilst seated close to the floor | By its tail while standing | In one hand above a table | By the scruff while walking
